  "construction": "Calibration at the neighbour exposure the 120 unsampled LGAs actually face.  The exposure is measured, not assumed: from the queen-contiguity graph over the 774 LGAs (built from data/public/boundaries/geoBoundaries-NGA-ADM2_simplified.geojson, 774 nodes, 2,230 edges, one component, zero isolates), e120 = adjacent pairs with both ends among the 120 LGAs holding no cluster, divided by 120.  200 of the 654 LGAs that hold at least one cluster are then built into five disjoint groups of 40, each group's internal adjacent-pair count brought to round(40*e120) by a random start plus a deterministic swap search, so every group sits within +-20% of e120.  A uniform random split could not: its expected internal pairs are only C(40,2)*2*2230/(774*773) = 5.81, about a quarter of the target.  Each group is one fit: that group's 40 LGAs' households are dropped and the identical household-level binomial model is refitted (ten design columns of eight covariates, BYM2 on the 774-node graph, IID cluster effect, INLA 25.10.19 defaults, no area-level covariates), then all 774 LGAs are predicted from prediction rows at each LGA's mean covariate profile taken from the FULL household file (covariates held known), cluster effect marginalised by the same 7-point Gauss-Hermite rule as scripts/lga_model.R.  The truth is the direct unweighted proportion from each held-out LGA's own households, with a cluster-robust ratio linearisation (strata = state, PSU = cluster) and median-design-effect imputation for single-cluster LGAs. z = (model_mean - direct)/sqrt(model_var + design_var).  Pass rule fixed before any fit and identical to T12 and T13: mean(z) in [-0.15,0.15], sd(z) in [0.85,1.15], share |z| <= 1.96 in [0.90,0.98].  Cluster counts and the observed/unobserved split come from data/derived/cluster_lga_fixed.csv and are cross-checked against the household file. Count-functional calibration is NOT tested: it needs joint draws per fold.",
